<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shen Yue</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">441–513</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shen Yue (441–513) was a Chinese historian, poet and statesman of the Southern Dynasties and one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eight-friends-of-jingling">Eight Friends of Jingling</a>. He compiled the Book of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>, the official history of the Liu Song dynasty, and with others formulated rules on the four tones of Chinese and the faults to avoid in verse, the basis of Yongming poetry. He helped Xiao Yan found the Liang dynasty in 502 and served him as a high minister.</p></div>
